speechtext:
1.	52:County courts at Barrie, Belleville, Brampton, Brantford, Brockville, Caledonia, Cayuga, Cobourg, Cornwall, Goderich, Guelph, Kingston, Kitchener, Lindsay, L'Orignal, Milton, Napanee, Orangeville, Owen Sound, Pembroke, Perth, Peterborough, Picton, Sarnia, Simcoe, Stratford, St. Thomas, Walkerton, Welland, Whitby, Windsor, Woodstock;
District courts at Bracebridge, Cochrane, Fort Frances, Gore Bay, Haileybury, Kenora, North Bay, Parry Sound, Port Arthur, Sault Ste. Marie;
General sessions of the peace at Chatham, Hamilton, Kitchener, London, Ottawa, Sudbury, St. Catharines, Timmins, Windsor;
Court of Canadian citizenship, Toronto.
2.	Information not available.
3.	Statutory fee set out in schedule B of Canadian Citizenship Act provides for a fee of $10 payable to the clerk of the court.
4.	Answered by No. 3; the clerk of the court of Canadian citizenship, Toronto, deposits the money received to the credit of the Receiver General of Canada.
